#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
fix_arena_sim.py — PreCon Arena AI vs AI batch runs (scope note section 6, as approved).

  * "AI plays A (batch)" on the Arena screen: run 1-500 games, live progress,
    a results panel (wins, first-player edge, game length, how games ended,
    mulligans, Act II/III rates and timing, climax accuracy, KOs, most/least
    used cards) and CSV export of the batch.
  * Mirror swap: the side whose turn begins is moved into the AI slot, so the
    one existing AI plays both decks unchanged.
  * Fast mode during a batch: delays under 3 s run at 0 ms (stall watchdogs
    keep theirs), the play screen isn't drawn, SFX muted — all restored after.
  * Seeded, replayable games: every game's seed is "<batch>#<n>" (in the CSV);
    enter it as the seed and run 1 game to replay that exact game.
  * Batch data stays in memory; your own Arena session log is not touched.

ALSO FIXES (found while building this): the AI's growing moves never grew.
fix_perturn_physical.py ticks growth in endTurn(), but the AI's turn ends
through endAiTurn() and never calls endTurn(). The tick now also runs there.

USAGE (repo root, after fix_precon_arena.py):
  python3 fix_arena_sim.py      then   python3 build.py
Writes src/game.src.html.bak.  Refuses to run twice.
"""
